// OpenFief's ticker confirmation contract (docs/DESIGN.md D-116, D-79).
//
// Some institutions, such as XTB's xStation export, name instruments by
// ticker and market only, with no ISIN (D-35). For each new ticker, the
// market-data connector looks the ISIN up by ticker and market and
// proposes it; the owner confirms it once, or enters it when the lookup
// found none. The rows of a ticker not confirmed yet wait as ingest
// problems, and the core books them once it is. The built-in UI hands the
// owner's confirmations to the core through TickerService, one owner-only
// service for this kind of entry (D-79), on the core's plugin port (D-115).
//
// Calling conventions are the AuthService's
// (proto/openfief/identity/v1/auth.proto), as in accounts.proto:
// - Every call carries the view plugin's projected ServiceAccount token
//   (audience openfief-core, D-27) as "Authorization: Bearer <token>"; a
//   call without one, or from a plugin that is not a view plugin, fails
//   with PERMISSION_DENIED.
// - Every request carries origin and the owner's session_token. A missing,
//   unknown, expired or revoked session fails with UNAUTHENTICATED; a
//   read-scoped session, or an origin off the core's allow-list, fails with
//   PERMISSION_DENIED.
// - An ISIN without a valid check digit fails with INVALID_ARGUMENT; a
//   ticker no connector instance reported with NOT_FOUND; a ticker already
//   confirmed with another ISIN with FAILED_PRECONDITION.

